      "message": "API approving because this is a module-lib API that is not accessible to apps.\n\nThe name is definitely unusual but it is required to be different from the existing ConnectivityFrameworkInitializer class because it must be in a different JAR which is loaded only on T+ devices.\n\nThere don\u0027t seem to be any better options at the moment:\n- Using \"33\" (i.e., the SDK version) is incorrect because T may not be 33.\n- We could use \"per-manager\" initializers instead of of \"per-Android-version\", and add NsdManagerInitializer, NetworkStatsManagerInitializer, EthernetManagerInitializer, IpSecManagerInitializer, etc. However:\n  - This would needlessly clutter the API surface\n  - It ouwl prevent us from adding any new ones after T ships because SystemServer.java is not updatable.",
